[32m+[m[32m// The transform stays where motion-paint's does — over lines a component has[m
[32m+[m[32m// already rendered — so a component never learns that a sweep is crossing it, and[m
[32m+[m[32m// every frame is byte-assertable. What is added here is column tracking: the line[m
[32m+[m[32m// is walked once, the background in effect is tracked as it goes, and a caller's[m
[32m+[m[32m// function is asked, per column, what the background should be instead.[m
